[debugger] Of the five failures, four are test defects and one is an API bug. All five diagnoses are recorded with high confidence, each backed by a direct probe. I created one probe booking (3933) and have deleted it.

- **05b Filter by checkin date (same day)** | "Booking checking in on that day is included" | **api_bug** | high | I created booking 3933 with checkin 2027-01-01. `GET /booking?checkin=2027-01-01` returns `[]`, while `?checkin=2026-12-31` returns it. The docs say the filter matches dates on or after the given date, but the API only returns later dates.
- **07 Update booking (full)** | "Status is 200" | **test_defect** | high | The request sends no `Cookie` or `Authorization` header. A PUT without auth returns 403 "Forbidden"; the same PUT with Basic auth returns 200 and totalprice 200. The docs require one of those two headers for PUT. Fix: add `Cookie: token={{token}}` or the Basic auth header.
- **07 Update booking (full)** | "Price is updated to 200" | **test_defect** | high | Same cause as above. The 403 body is the plain text "Forbidden", so reading it as JSON fails with "Unexpected token 'F'".
- **08 Update booking (partial)** | "Only additionalneeds changed" | **test_defect** (knock-on from 07) | high | The PATCH itself worked (200, additionalneeds = "Late checkout"). totalprice is still 150 only because the PUT in 07 was rejected. It should pass once 07 is fixed.
- **09 Delete booking** | "Deleted (status 200)" | **test_defect** | high | The docs give 201 Created as the success response for delete, and deleting my probe booking returned 201 "Created". The test should expect 201.

I saved new lessons to the knowledge base for the checkin filter, the PUT auth requirement and the DELETE status code.

